Z||000000||Voytek||10-30-2001||05:23 PM||||Hey<BR>Someone who used to live in Saskatchewan (goes by Steve) said you may be able to give me info on how many Fieros there are at Amigo's in Clavet.  Also, I'd be interested in knowing if it's worth taking a drive from Calgary (I'd like to buy a few odds and ends) or if the cars are completely picked through.<P>Your help is appreciated.<BR>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||loafer87gt||10-30-2001||06:46 PM||||Oh, hey man. Last time I was at Amigos they had around 10 Fieros there. Most of them were in pretty rough shape and suffered from really bad water and sun damage. What sort of parts are you looking for? From what I remember, most of the interior parts were light grey(almost bleached white by the sun), and tan. I wasn't able to find any interior parts that were the same medium grey as in my 87 GT. As far as the body panels go, most of them are in pretty rough shape as the cars are all write offs. If it would help you out, I could take a drive out there sometime next week and snap some digital camera shots of the cars for you, Clevette is only about a twenty minute drive from Saskatoon. Let me know,||||reg||1
Z||000002||Voytek||10-31-2001||10:46 AM||||Hey<BR>Thanks a lot for the info.  I've actually called there yesterday and was looking for some parts.  First, they said they have about 5 Fieros now.  Second, just as an example, they wanted like $45 bucks for a center console.  This may not sound like much, but I picked one up for someone in Calgary about 2 years ago at Pick Your Part for $7 bucks.<P>I guess now I'm starting to think that for the few parts I'd like to get, it may not be worth the 6-7 hour drive from Calgary.<P>I appreciate you willing to drive out there and help me out, though.  Maybe I'll try this again in the spring when the weather's a bit nicer and I feel like going for a drive.<P>Thank you!<BR>Voytek||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haspers8||10-31-2001||05:29 PM|||| Holy crap......they only have 5 left.  They had one whole line along the west fence.  I counted something like 30, but that was 3 years ago.  Ah well what can you do.<P>Later <BR>Steve<BR>85 indigo IMSA V8||||reg||13
